easa-rules pack: content licence
================================

1. ATTRIBUTION STATEMENT
------------------------

This pack is derived from material of the European Union Aviation Safety
Agency (EASA): AMC 20-115D, Airborne Software Development Assurance Using
EUROCAE ED-12 and RTCA DO-178, created by ED Decision 2017/020/R, and
AMC 20-152A, Development Assurance for Airborne Electronic Hardware, created
by ED Decision 2020/010/R, both read as consolidated in AMC-20 Amendment 23
(ED Decision 2022/001/R, June 2023 Easy Access Rules compilation). What ships
here is a set of reconstructed reference notes built from those sources; it is
not an official EASA text, EASA did not take part in making it, and nothing in
it should be read as an endorsement by EASA.

2. SOURCE IDENTIFICATION
------------------------

Copyright holder for every source below: European Union Aviation Safety
Agency (EASA).

-   S1  AMC 20-115D, Airborne Software Development Assurance Using EUROCAE
        ED-12 and RTCA DO-178. Created by ED Decision 2017/020/R of
        19 October 2017 (AMC-20 Amendment 14). Consolidated basis: AMC-20
        Amendment 23 (June 2023). Section slice EAR pp. 416-430, including
        GM1 to GM3.
-   S2  AMC 20-152A, Development Assurance for Airborne Electronic Hardware.
        Created by ED Decision 2020/010/R of 17 July 2020 (AMC-20 Amendment
        19). Consolidated basis: AMC-20 Amendment 23 (June 2023). Section
        slice EAR pp. 497-517.
-   S3  Easy Access Rules for Acceptable Means of Compliance for Airworthiness
        of Products, Parts and Appliances (AMC-20), Amendment 23, published
        June 2023. Retrieval carrier only: the compilation supplied the page
        images the S1 and S2 slices were cut from; it is not ingested whole.
-   S5/S6 (decision anchors, taken together)  ED Decision 2017/020/R of
        19 October 2017, the instrument creating AMC 20-115D, and ED Decision
        2020/010/R of 17 July 2020, the instrument creating AMC 20-152A. Cited
        in this pack for the decision numbers and dates only.

Note on the 2017 instrument: the footer of the ED Decision 2017/020/R PDF uses
the agency's older name, European Aviation Safety Agency (without "Union");
the copyright holder is the same agency throughout.

3. SOURCE LINKS
---------------

Document-library pages (preferred identifiers; file download ids live in the
build manifest, not here):

-   S1 and S5: https://www.easa.europa.eu/en/document-library/agency-decisions/ed-decision-2017020r
-   S2 and S6: https://www.easa.europa.eu/en/document-library/agency-decisions/ed-decision-2020010r
-   S3: https://www.easa.europa.eu/en/document-library/easy-access-rules/easy-access-rules-acceptable-means-compliance-airworthiness

4. LICENCE BASIS
----------------

The EASA copyright page (https://www.easa.europa.eu/en/copyright-disclaimer)
states that reproduction is authorised, provided the source is acknowledged,
unless otherwise stated. The ED Decision 2017/020/R and 2020/010/R PDFs carry
"All rights reserved" footers and present themselves as proprietary EASA
publications. The Easy Access Rules AMC-20 compilation (Amendment 23) is
marked as not an official publication. Each source keeps its own basis, and
commercial use stays pending a per-document determination.

5. NATURE OF THIS PACK
----------------------

Everything under packs/easa-rules/ is a reconstructed reference note: the
source sections are restructured, paraphrased, and summarised in this pack's
own organisation and words, with short defined terms only. Direct quotation is
capped at two sentences per item and is used sparingly. Objective tables and
lists are never pasted in from any source, including by optical character
recognition; tables in the chapters are original summaries, and any column
that would point at paywalled standard text says so instead.

6. NON-ENDORSEMENT
------------------

EASA does not endorse this pack. The European Union does not endorse this pack.

7. EAR DISCLAIMER
-----------------

The Easy Access Rules compilation that served as the retrieval carrier for S1
and S2 (S3 above) is published with a disclaimer stating that it is not an
official publication and that EASA accepts no liability for its contents; that
disclaimer carries over to any use of the carrier, and the official text of
AMC 20-115D and AMC 20-152A remains the annexes to ED Decision 2017/020/R and
ED Decision 2020/010/R as amended and consolidated.

8. EXCLUDED MATERIAL
--------------------

The following are named in this pack for identification only; none of their
text is reproduced, and none is licensed to this pack:

-   RTCA DO-178C and EUROCAE ED-12C, and the supplement set: RTCA DO-330,
    DO-331, DO-332, DO-333 and EUROCAE ED-215 to ED-218.
-   RTCA DO-254 and EUROCAE ED-80.
-   EASA logos, crests, and other official emblems.
-   The full Easy Access Rules AMC-20 PDF (S3 carrier): only the two section
    slices were read; the compilation is not redistributed.
-   The full Amendment 23 annex as a standalone redistribution.
-   The Part-21 Easy Access Rules volume (outside this pack's scope).
-   AMC 20-193 (multi-core processors), AMC 20-189 (open problem reports), and AMC 20-170 (guidance on AI assurance):
    named as pointers only, not covered by this release.
-   S7 (the wider AMC-20 material beyond the two sections): out of this
    release.

9. SCOPE OF THIS FILE
---------------------

This licence file governs the content of packs/easa-rules/: SKILL.md,
chapters/, glossary.md, and cheatsheet.md. The repository tooling, installers,
and CI are licensed separately under the repository MIT licence and are not
covered by this file.

